From 6d6c743eca2729d16c5cfd63ad55de3c4dd026eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 02:58:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/29] Force every guard log line to the storage, and sample
 once a second

The first crash on the phone left a log that stopped at 22:33:06 with the
reboot recorded at 22:34:23. The obvious reading is that the watchdog stopped
sampling; it did not. File.appendText puts the bytes in the page cache, the
writeback timer is up to thirty seconds behind, and a kernel panic takes the
page cache with it - so every line written in the seconds before the panic was
gone, and the log ended a minute and a half before the event it exists to
record.

Each line is now written and fsync'd, which costs microseconds on a file this
quiet and puts the last line before a panic where it can be read afterwards.
With that paid for, the periodic sample can be every second instead of every
four, and every 500 ms once anything is out of the ordinary: the seconds before
a panic are the only seconds that matter afterwards, and a four-second gap is
most of them.

Also documents it in docs/gpu-safety.md, because a log that loses the end is a
log that lies about what the watchdog was doing.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
